course: dictionary
lesson: 6529
title: Nest: a home, and more
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A nest is a home that birds build to lay their eggs and raise their young. Other animals make nests too, such as wasps, ants, mice and squirrels. Nest can be a noun (a nest) or a verb (to nest).
explain: Use the words around the word to find its meaning. «Birds may nest in a nest box in spring.» Nest is a verb here, so it means to build or live in a nest. Spring is the clue, because that is when birds are busy with their homes.
explain: Nest can also mean things that fit inside each other. «The bowls nest together in the cupboard» tells you they fit snugly inside each other, like nesting dolls. When you meet nest, ask: is it a home, an action, or things that fit inside each other?
fact: A nest is a home that birds build to lay eggs and raise their young.
fact: Birds use twigs, grass, mud and feathers to build their nests.
fact: Other animals make nests too, such as wasps, ants, mice and squirrels.
fact: «Nest» can be a noun (a nest) or a verb (to nest, to build or live in a nest).
fact: Things that nest fit inside each other, like nesting dolls.
exercise: «Birds may nest in a nest box in spring.» What does nest mean in this sentence? | To hide underground | To sing loudly in the trees | *To build or live in a nest | To fly away to hot countries
exercise: Which animal makes a nest? | Horse | Goldfish | *Squirrel | Cow
exercise: «The bowls nest together in the cupboard.» What does nest mean in this sentence? | Sit in a tree | *Fit snugly inside each other | Be made of wood | Be very heavy
test: «The kingdom of God is like a tiny mustard seed that grows into a large plant where birds nest.» What does nest mean here? | To dig for gold | To swim under water | To buy food | *To build or live in a nest
test: A bird builds a nest to lay what? | Stones | *Eggs | Shoes | Books
exam: Mia says nest is a bird word only, so nesting dolls must be a mistake. Is she right? | Yes, nest only means a bird's home | *No, wasps, ants, mice and squirrels nest too, and things that fit inside each other nest | Yes, but only in spring | No, a nest is a hard, round stone
